    <statement><p>Without calculation, decide if each of the integrals
below are positive, negative, or zero.  Let W be the 
solid bounded by  <m>z = \sqrt{x^2 + y^2}</m> and <m>z = 2</m>.</p>
<p><ol>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle \iiint\limits_W \left( z - \sqrt{x^2+y^2} \right) \, dV</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle \iiint\limits_W \left( z - 2 \right) \, dV</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle \iiint\limits_W e^{-xyz} \, dV</m></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
